# 1-based lines to bookmark. Each sits INSIDE a construct the profile claims to
# understand, so a broken `containers` shows up as a missing breadcrumb.
#
# Lines are chosen to be structurally distinct from their siblings. Codemark
# refuses a bookmark whose generated query matches more than one node, so a
# statement with an identically-shaped sibling is not a usable anchor (the
# Scala profile hit exactly this).

# Inside a constructor inside a class: class InvoiceError > def __init__.
# The `super().__init__(...)` call is the only call in that body — its sibling
# is an assignment, so the query stays unambiguous.
34

# Inside a conditional inside a method inside a class:
# class Invoice > def compute > if not self.payable.
# Proves `method` is a real container, not just a landmark.
70

# Inside a method in a class nested in a class:
# class Invoice > class Draft > def promote.
# Proves class-in-class containment — the chain Kotlin cannot express.
124

# The deepest chain here: a function nested in a method, in a nested class, in
# a class — class Invoice > class Draft > def discount > def apply.
# This is the line that proves `function` belongs in `containers`.
129
